{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Ready on the cross-account probe whenever you are. The procedure:\n\n1. You: `codex logout`, then log in as the free-tier account.\n2. Tell me \"go\" and I'll run `node scripts/probe-encrypted-reasoning.mjs` against the July 18 donor rollout (the blob stays on disk from your main account — that's exactly the cross-account condition we want).\n3. Reading the result: marker recalled → blobs are portable across accounts (global-key hypothesis); a 4xx specifically on the reasoning item → per-account keying, teammate replay is dead; an auth/plan error before any turn runs → inconclusive, since the free tier may not include Codex access at all — that's the one caveat, and we'll be able to tell the difference from the error text.\n\nOn the coerce/match setting — good instinct, but the design space collapses more than you'd think, which I've noted in the roadmap (committed). The \"coerce\" lane for foreign reasoning *already exists and is always on*: it's the `[visible thinking]` text folding, which is the only safe representation since fake ciphertext can't be forged and is confirmed-unsafe to attempt. So the only genuine switch is whether provider-matched encrypted replay is on or off. A `cx→cl→cx` session under replay-on would naturally carry both: replayed blobs for the Codex legs, folded text for the Claude leg — your out-of-distribution worry applies only to the folded text, which is the status quo you've already been running with.\n\n**And yes — the original goal is finished, plus most of the list.** You asked for a priority-ranked TODO list informed by your intent and a cledger impact review; both were delivered, and then you had me execute. Where the ranked list stands now:\n\n| Item | Status |\n|---|---|\n| P0: verify interactive resume | **Done** — pty harness + `--manual` mode; you visually confirmed both TUIs |\n| P0: absorb cledger 0.8.0 read side effects | **Done** — sequenced reads